  "metaDescription": "Gibran Rakabuming Raka has resigned as the Vice President of Indonesia. President Prabowo Subianto and Gibran provided differing reasons for the departure.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "Gibran Rakabuming Raka officially vacated his position as the Vice President of Indonesia on November 12, 2026.",
    "President Prabowo Subianto cited educational and constitutional requirements as the reason, while Gibran denied that the resignation is linked to academic credentials.",
    "Government officials and political figures, including the Governor of Yogyakarta, have emphasized that state operations remain normal."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "On November 12, 2026, Gibran Rakabuming Raka resigned from his position as Vice President of Indonesia. Following a day of final official engagements, which included a meeting with President Prabowo Subianto and a visit to the parliamentary complex, Gibran expressed gratitude to the President for the trust placed in him. Public statements regarding the cause of his resignation vary; President Prabowo Subianto stated that the departure is tied to educational systems and constitutional compliance. Conversely, Gibran publicly refuted claims that his exit is related to his academic credentials. In the wake of the resignation, various political parties have urged for a cabinet evaluation, though government representatives maintain that national governance continues to function as usual. Prominent figures, such as the Sultan of Yogyakarta, have refrained from speculating on a potential successor.",
